1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,410
Last time, we pulled two strips.

2
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:05,980
Fabric held more weights: it is stronger than paper.

3
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:09,490
A glass cup broke easily: glass is fragile.

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,480
Now, test three: bend!

5
00:00:14,729 --> 00:00:15,949
Lock in first.

6
00:00:16,229 --> 00:00:18,979
A little caterpillar is hiding in this video.

7
00:00:19,229 --> 00:00:20,469
Can you spot it?

8
00:00:21,043 --> 00:00:22,373
Today you'll learn:

9
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:24,340
What flexibility means.

10
00:00:24,545 --> 00:00:26,255
Flexible or rigid.

11
00:00:26,453 --> 00:00:28,793
Strong is not the same as flexible.

12
00:00:30,474 --> 00:00:33,004
Round one: the question from last time!

13
00:00:33,284 --> 00:00:35,284
Which one can bend without breaking?

14
00:00:35,564 --> 00:00:37,054
One, the rubber band.

15
00:00:37,324 --> 00:00:38,914
Two, the ice-cream stick.

16
00:00:39,204 --> 00:00:40,514
Show me your fingers!

17
00:00:43,987 --> 00:00:44,967
Locked in!

18
00:00:45,095 --> 00:00:45,975
Two.

19
00:00:46,135 --> 00:00:46,965
The stick.

20
00:00:47,325 --> 00:00:49,585
Wood is strong, so it will not break.

21
00:00:49,631 --> 00:00:50,241
One!

22
00:00:50,401 --> 00:00:52,261
I bend rubber bands all day!

23
00:00:52,316 --> 00:00:53,046
One!

24
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:54,954
Look closer.

25
00:00:55,534 --> 00:00:57,124
The rubber band bends.

26
00:00:57,694 --> 00:00:58,654
In half.

27
00:00:59,224 --> 00:01:00,454
Into a twist.

28
00:01:01,034 --> 00:01:02,084
No crack.

29
00:01:02,664 --> 00:01:04,014
It does not break.

30
00:01:04,514 --> 00:01:06,214
Now the ice-cream stick.

31
00:01:06,784 --> 00:01:08,314
It bends, just a little.

32
00:01:08,934 --> 00:01:09,784
Listen.

33
00:01:10,374 --> 00:01:11,714
A crack opens.

34
00:01:12,344 --> 00:01:13,174
Snap!

35
00:01:13,744 --> 00:01:14,774
It breaks.

36
00:01:17,264 --> 00:01:18,564
The answer is one.

37
00:01:18,834 --> 00:01:20,024
The rubber band!

38
00:01:20,076 --> 00:01:20,796
Oh!

39
00:01:21,076 --> 00:01:22,186
It snapped!

40
00:01:22,235 --> 00:01:23,225
One finger?

41
00:01:23,545 --> 00:01:24,735
One finger up!

42
00:01:25,936 --> 00:01:27,096
Say it with me!

43
00:01:27,804 --> 00:01:32,144
The flexibility of a material is its ability to bend without breaking.

44
00:01:36,847 --> 00:01:38,137
Say it with me!

45
00:01:38,851 --> 00:01:42,301
Materials that bend easily without breaking are flexible.

46
00:01:42,821 --> 00:01:45,861
Materials that break easily when bent are rigid.

47
00:01:48,935 --> 00:01:51,115
A rubber tile bends: flexible.

48
00:01:51,405 --> 00:01:54,575
A ceramic tile breaks when it is bent: rigid.

49
00:01:54,922 --> 00:01:56,152
Be a rubber band!

50
00:01:56,432 --> 00:01:57,412
Shrink down.

51
00:01:57,692 --> 00:01:58,622
Quietly.

52
00:02:00,911 --> 00:02:03,941
You are a rubber band, at the chicken rice stall.

53
00:02:04,614 --> 00:02:06,064
Fingers pick you up.

54
00:02:06,864 --> 00:02:08,374
They bend you in half.

55
00:02:09,038 --> 00:02:11,178
They loop you round a packet of rice.

56
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:13,788
You bend at every corner.

57
00:02:15,444 --> 00:02:17,464
At home, fingers pull you off.

58
00:02:18,254 --> 00:02:19,434
You bend again.

59
00:02:20,093 --> 00:02:21,113
No crack.

60
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:22,953
No snap.

61
00:02:23,743 --> 00:02:25,043
You are flexible!

62
00:02:27,253 --> 00:02:28,533
Now I am hungry!

63
00:02:29,186 --> 00:02:30,336
Look closer.

64
00:02:30,936 --> 00:02:32,026
Three tubes.

65
00:02:32,596 --> 00:02:34,456
The same weight hangs on each.

66
00:02:35,026 --> 00:02:36,946
The rubber tube bends the most.

67
00:02:37,516 --> 00:02:39,426
The metal tube bends the least.

68
00:02:39,637 --> 00:02:43,437
Rubber tubes can bend more than plastic tubes without breaking.

69
00:02:43,697 --> 00:02:47,357
Plastic tubes can bend more than metal tubes without breaking.

70
00:02:51,664 --> 00:02:52,554
My notes!

71
00:02:52,684 --> 00:02:55,894
One: rubber bends the most, so it is the most flexible.

72
00:02:55,954 --> 00:02:58,824
Two: paper bends easily, so paper is strong.

73
00:02:58,904 --> 00:03:02,194
Three: metal bends the least, so it is the least flexible.

74
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:03,370
Showdown!

75
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:04,810
Double points.

76
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,700
One line has a mistake.

77
00:03:06,990 --> 00:03:08,750
Line one, two, or three?

78
00:03:09,050 --> 00:03:10,520
Show me with your fingers.

79
00:03:16,995 --> 00:03:17,975
Locked in!

80
00:03:18,103 --> 00:03:18,733
Two!

81
00:03:18,863 --> 00:03:19,953
Paper bends.

82
00:03:19,973 --> 00:03:21,913
But it tore with only three weights!

83
00:03:21,961 --> 00:03:22,851
Two.

84
00:03:23,051 --> 00:03:25,441
Bending and tearing are different tests.

85
00:03:25,495 --> 00:03:26,095
Oops!

86
00:03:26,752 --> 00:03:29,432
Paper bends easily: it is flexible.

87
00:03:29,782 --> 00:03:32,352
But it tears easily: it is not strong.

88
00:03:32,722 --> 00:03:35,592
Strong and flexible are two different properties.

89
00:03:35,728 --> 00:03:36,768
Two fingers?

90
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:38,938
Put up two more on your score hand!

91
00:03:39,496 --> 00:03:40,601
Say it with us!

92
00:03:41,261 --> 00:03:42,623
Physical property!

93
00:03:42,841 --> 00:03:44,244
Measure or observe!

94
00:03:47,661 --> 00:03:48,421
Strength!

95
00:03:48,441 --> 00:03:50,642
Pull it, push it: no break, no tear!

96
00:03:54,061 --> 00:03:55,223
Flexibility!

97
00:03:55,641 --> 00:03:57,122
Bend without breaking!

98
00:04:01,216 --> 00:04:02,686
Show me your score hand!

99
00:04:02,966 --> 00:04:04,016
More than one?

100
00:04:04,316 --> 00:04:05,676
You beat the Buddies.

101
00:04:05,976 --> 00:04:07,036
Three fingers?

102
00:04:07,306 --> 00:04:08,316
High five!

103
00:04:08,821 --> 00:04:10,441
Did you spot the caterpillar?

104
00:04:10,721 --> 00:04:13,821
It was on the handrail of the slide, bending along!

105
00:04:14,091 --> 00:04:15,391
Tell someone at home.

106
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:17,490
Next time, water!

107
00:04:17,770 --> 00:04:19,240
A metal spoon sinks.

108
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,390
But a giant metal ship floats!

109
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:24,220
What is inside the ship that helps it to float?

110
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,440
One, wood.

111
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:26,640
Two, air.

112
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,150
Three, more metal.

113
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,750
Lock in your answer!

114
00:04:29,805 --> 00:04:31,945
A ship is heavier than a million spoons!

115
00:04:32,005 --> 00:04:32,795
How?

116
00:04:33,516 --> 00:04:35,716
Let's read today's key words together!

117
00:04:36,006 --> 00:04:36,766
Ready?

118
00:04:37,103 --> 00:04:38,028
Flexibility.

119
00:04:39,767 --> 00:04:40,717
Flexible.

120
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,010
Rigid.

121
00:04:44,382 --> 00:04:45,322
Well done!

122
00:04:46,304 --> 00:04:47,405
Say it with us!

123
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:48,955
Ready?

124
00:04:49,078 --> 00:04:49,738
One!

125
00:04:50,078 --> 00:04:50,778
two!

126
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:52,258
Now you know!
